      "actualScope": "The selected commands are ContainerHullSystem, IsAdmissible, hull_integralRegion, hullAdmissible, and hullFamily. ContainerHullSystem supplies one HullSystem for every packet and label-set index. It also supplies admissibility of each designated integral region. IsAdmissible requires each region to belong to the corresponding supplied admissible class. The integral region is a fixed point of its supplied hull. This proves preservation of the finite-exception condition under the packetwise operation hullAdmissible. That operation is defined on every AdmissibleRegion without an IsAdmissible premise; the premise is needed for the unselected inclusion and monotonicity results. hullFamily applies this operation at every label-set index. These definitions preserve the indices. They do not construct arithmetic hull systems or identify the arbitrary component rings with the paper’s fields. The prerequisite HullSystem has an arbitrary admissible class and a supplied total hull map. Outside that class its values are unconstrained. Its hull class uses unit multipliers and may be smaller than all such regions. Those choices differ from the full-space branch and nonzero field multipliers in the paper. The leastness and admissibility fields are supplied assumptions."
    },
