      "actualScope": "The selected commands are LogVolumeData, globalVol, and processionVol. LogVolumeData supplies real-valued component and packet functions on all subsets. It requires strictly positive place weights whose sum on each fiber is one. It records zero component values on finite-place integral subsets, a +log(p) law for preimages under multiplication by p on unit-scaled integral subsets, and zero on a designated archimedean subset archBall. The type of archBall does not assert that it is a Hermitian ball. The packet integral region has zero value. On a product region with every component nonempty, the packet value is the sum of component values weighted by the product of the place weights over labels. The law includes no compactness, measurability, or finite-positive-measure premise. These are actual interface conditions, not a construction of Haar measure. The functions have values on empty and unbounded sets, but no general monotonicity field is present. globalVol uses a finite sum over all rational places; the region equals the integral region outside a finite set, so the summand vanishes there. processionVol divides the sum of global values by the procession length. A zero length is permitted; Lean’s real division gives zero in that case. The code does not identify its weights with the paper’s degree formulas. In particular, the header’s intended [K_v:Q_vQ]/[K:Q] formula differs from the inverse-extension-degree formula on paper page 94. Positive weights with fiber sum one do not prove this missing arithmetic identification. Global principal-element invariance and equality with arithmetic degree are not fields of this interface.",
