      "actualSourceConsumer": "Iut.Theorem110Invariants.theorem110",
      "sourceCommandsPreserved": true,
      "rootGraphMembership": false,
      "canonicalC22Connected": false,
      "actualScope": "PrimeToOrder ℓ n is Nat.Coprime ℓ n for arbitrary natural numbers ℓ and n. Its definition does not require that ℓ be prime. OrderedTateParameter extends an arbitrary NormedField TateParameter with a supplied positive natural number orderNat. The structure itself contains no equation relating orderNat to q, a valuation, the series, or the curve. Its PrimeToOrder predicate applies Nat.Coprime to ℓ and orderNat. The selected decidability instances implement these predicates. No theorem here asserts the existence of a suitable prime or proves that a particular prime satisfies the condition. The paper also assumes coprimality with residue characteristics; that is separate from this predicate. The later toOrdered construction supplies a particular norm-based order under a uniformizer assumption, but does not change what an arbitrary OrderedTateParameter contains."
    },
