      "actualScope": "For a TateParameter t over an arbitrary NormedField K, eisenstein k is the total infinite sum over n≥0 of (n+1)^k q^(n+1)/(1-q^(n+1)). The selected definitions set a₄=-5·eisenstein 3 and a₆=-(5·eisenstein 3+7·eisenstein 5)/12. tateCurve is a WeierstrassCurve with a₁=1, a₂=a₃=0, and these a₄,a₆. The four definitions require neither completeness nor an ultrametric norm. Their infinite sum uses Lean’s total tsum; these definitions alone do not prove convergence. The source file proves summability separately under completeness and an ultrametric norm, but those proofs are not selected here. In characteristics dividing 12, division by the field element 12 follows Lean’s total division convention. There is no characteristic restriction in these definitions. The result is a WeierstrassCurve, with no selected smoothness, discriminant-nonvanishing, elliptic-curve, uniformization, or identity theorem identifying it with GenEll’s E. Calling the declaration tateCurve does not establish those bridges."
