      "actualScope": "IsUniformizer π requires π≠0, ‖π‖<1, and an integer exponent representation ‖x‖=‖π‖^n for every unit x. This is a condition on a normed field; the selected statements do not require completeness or an ultrametric norm. The selected lemmas give ‖π‖>0 and log‖π‖<0. For a TateParameter t, exists_norm_q_eq_zpow obtains an exponent from the generation field. orderZ chooses such an integer. norm_q_eq_zpow gives its defining equation, and orderZ_pos proves positivity from the strict norm bounds. toOrdered sets orderNat to the natural-number conversion of this positive integer and preserves t. Positivity makes this conversion exact, although integer-to-natural conversion is generally truncated. This unit does not construct a uniformizer for an arithmetic completion. It does not prove that the norm-derived exponent agrees with the paper’s valuation, a special-fiber component count, or the order of a curve identified with the paper’s E. Those arithmetic identifications require additional input."
